# .sastignore - SAST Findings Suppression File
# This file is used to suppress SAST (Static Application Security Testing) findings
# that have been reviewed and determined to be false positives or acceptable risks.
#
# Format: Each line should contain a rule ID or file pattern to ignore
# Lines starting with # are comments
#
# Examples:
#   - Ignore a specific rule: eslint/detect-object-injection
#   - Ignore findings in a file: src/test/**
#   - Ignore a specific finding: semgrep:javascript.lang.security.audit.detect-non-literal-regexp
#
# Documentation: https://docs.gitlab.com/ee/user/application_security/sast/#customizing-the-sast-settings

# Test files - security findings in test code are generally lower risk
src/**/*.spec.ts
# Add specific rule suppressions below after reviewing findings
# Example: semgrep:javascript.lang.security.audit.path-traversal

